# Packaged builds. Deliberately at the top of the tree rather than inside a
# build directory: an archive you are about to send someone should be somewhere
# you can see it.
dist/

# Build trees
build/
build-*/
cmake-build-*/
out/
_deps/
CMakeUserPresets.json

# Working directory for archives dropped in from elsewhere, backups taken
# before applying them, and the out-of-tree build trees. Nothing in here is
# source; it is measured in gigabytes.
.incoming/

# The generated build stamp lives in the build tree, but keep it out by name in
# case someone configures in place.
build_info.hpp

# Editors and tooling
.idea/
.vscode/
.cache/
compile_commands.json
*.swp
*~

# macOS
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
._*

# Vendor manuals in every form: the PDFs and compiled help they came as, and
# the markdown they were converted to. Bizerba's documentation is Bizerba's,
# and this repository is public.
#
# The tooling does read docs/markdown/ -- gen_registry.py generates the token
# table from GxNet.md -- so keep a copy locally. What survives here instead is
# docs/*-notes.md, which cites the originals by symbolic name, subfunction code
# and quote precisely so that they can be searched without being shipped.
docs/original/
docs/Help/
docs/markdown/
# Vendor sample code and templates: C++/C# examples, Excel macros, SAP
# transports, XML file-interface samples. Third-party source, and the facts
# worth keeping out of it are recorded in the code and the notes instead.
docs/Samples/

# The service built on this library: its design, its API notes, its deployment.
# Business logic tied to one installation and one ERP, and none of it is what
# this repository is for. Create files here freely; they stay local.
docs/service/

# Captures and logs pulled off the server while debugging
*.commlog
*.log
